Turnip on mondrian: let the kernel choose the IOVAs

Measured 2026-11-19: with 0382 in, Turnip enumerates the A730 and vkCreateDevice
goes one step further, then fails in BO init:

    TU: error: MSM_INFO_SET_IOVA failed! -78 (No such file or directory)
    TU: error: tu_device.cc:2615: BO init (VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY)

MSM_INFO_SET_IOVA in MondrianGPU answers kIOReturnUnsupported for any address
but the buffer's own, so Turnip's client-chosen IOVA path cannot work here; the
kernel already answers MSM_INFO_GET_IOVA, which is the path kgsl devices take.

--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm_msm.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm_msm.cc
@@ -1085,8 +1085,19 @@
       goto fail;
    }
 
+#if defined(__APPLE__)
+   /*
+    * mondrian's kernel is the IOVA authority: MSM_INFO_SET_IOVA accepts only
+    * the address the kernel already gave the buffer and answers EINVAL for any
+    * other, which Turnip reads as "BO init failed" and turns into no device at
+    * all (measured 2026-11-19). Ask for the kernel's address instead.
+    */
+   device->has_set_iova = false;
+   (void)tu_drm_get_va_prop(device, &device->va_start, &device->va_size);
+#else
    device->has_set_iova = !tu_drm_get_va_prop(device, &device->va_start,
                                               &device->va_size);
+#endif
    device->has_raytracing = tu_drm_get_raytracing(device);
 
    device->has_preemption = tu_drm_has_preemption(device);
